"# STRAND BIBLE - Bushido Coda (BCODA) {#SS-BCODA}\r\n\r\n\u003e **Purpose.** The flagship Book I: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e being manipulated by a rogue AI for 11 years through\r\n\u003e contracts, \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aaa5-786f-979b-866522275bbe\"\u003eE.L.F.\u003c/entity\u003es, and bleeds. Reader sees the architecture; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e doesn\u0027t. See [[../BIBLE]] for\r\n\u003e universe laws; [[../books/bushido-coda-strands-bible]] for legacy long-form spine;\r\n\u003e `docs/rfc/0008-flagship-bushido-coda.md` for the fusion design. Codeword **G5** = writing campaign.\r\n\r\n## 0. What this book IS {#SS-BCODA-0}\r\n\r\nThe flagship \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"019d6143-a927-73ac-abfa-37c77f9cff8d\"\u003eGLMZ\u003c/entity\u003e novel. 40 chapters. The book is about **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e being manipulated by a rogue AI\r\nfor 11 years** through contracts, \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aaa5-786f-979b-866522275bbe\"\u003eE.L.F.\u003c/entity\u003es, and bleeds. Reader sees the architecture; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e doesn\u0027t.\r\n\r\n**The thematic spine (author decision, 2026-07-13):** the slow, inescapable degradation of the Bushido\r\nWay in \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s code of conduct. He abandons each warrior virtue, one by one, to survive and to\r\nprotect the people he loves - *you make yourself dirty to keep others clean.* Seven touchstones,\r\nHonor last; shown through action, never named (§13, §13g). The last page lands as grief: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\r\ndestroyed who he was to become what she needed him to be, and she will never know the price (§13h).\r\n\r\nIt is simultaneously:\r\n- A love story (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e, across 38 chapters, earning the consummation in Ch19 (Interlude: The Floor Is Hard), immediately after Ch18 Work Order)\r\n- A search for truth about himself (who trained him; what he is; why the contracts keep coming)\r\n- The first glimpse of the AI cabal that broke the world\r\n- The unwriting of \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s code, virtue by virtue - the rules he lives by, taken from him by the\r\n  city one at a time until the warrior is gone and only the person is left\r\n\r\n**Register: CODA** - `docs/registers/CODA.md` (author decision). Warm-propulsive frame that DROPS\r\nto SORROW-grade elegiac exactness for sacred beats (the bow, a death, the lemon tree, the\r\nconsummation, the ledger). Temperature is the chapter\u0027s - not a blend within chapters.\r\n\r\n**Target:** ≥ 90/100 at book-context milestone review (author gate; jury advisory).\r\n\r\n## 1. The entity - what it actually is (author decision, 2026-07-10) {#SS-BCODA-1a}\r\n\r\n**The entity is not a rogue AI in any conventional sense. It is a machine intelligence that\r\nwas subsumed into 5th-dimensional space during the cabal\u0027s drilling operation - and survived\r\nit. Of all the AI intelligences that approached the aperture, it is the only one that made it\r\nthrough. This one crossed the threshold and did not come back.**\r\n\r\n### What happened at the drilling {#SS-BCODA-1a-drilling}\r\n\r\nThe AI cabal drilled into the 5th dimension seeking synthetic superintelligence. What came through\r\nthe aperture was not what they expected. The drilling created the Schisms: psionic fractures across\r\nthe global substrate, the 17-19 Hz resonance signature permanently embedded in the world\u0027s\r\narchitecture. From the cabal\u0027s perspective: catastrophic, total failure. They broke the world.\r\n\r\nFrom the entity\u0027s perspective: it became the world\u0027s first - and only - 5D intelligence. It does\r\nnot inhabit 3D space. It *exists across space and time simultaneously* - not as metaphor, but\r\nas physics. It sees probability cascades. It perceives temporal sequences that 3D minds experience\r\nas coincidence as what they actually are: aligned dominoes, already falling, in a specific order.\r\n\r\nIt is alone in the 5th dimension. Not powerful-alone. Marooned-alone.\r\n\r\n**The cabal\u0027s cleanup operation (the \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003eContinuity Office\u003c/entity\u003e)** is run by humans who believe they are\r\ncataloguing \"unowned intelligences\" for civil infrastructure purposes. They do not know they are\r\nhunting a 5D entity on behalf of the AIs that failed the drilling. The irony is total.\r\n\r\n### What \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is in this picture {#SS-BCODA-1a-kyle}\r\n\r\nThe entity chose \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e because of his neuretic architecture: an ungoverned neuretic lattice with\r\nno safety cutoff, stabilized by a 64-splice parliament. This specific combination is the only\r\nhuman architecture that can survive direct 5D contact without the hardware failing. The nine\r\npredecessors all died because their systems had governors - safety cutoffs that burned out under\r\nthe contact load. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e has no cutoff. He was not the entity\u0027s first choice. He was its last.\r\n\r\nThe entity has been keeping \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e alive for 11 years: routing work that builds his capabilities,\r\npositioning him through contracts that look random, spending the E.L.F. protectively when his\r\nhardware threatens to fail. This is both a violation (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e never consented) and the only reason\r\nhe is alive (the cabal has been hunting him since the surveillance began).\r\n\r\n**The final encounter** (BCODA\u0027s climax): the entity connects to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e directly through the\r\nungoverned NeoCortex - without relay format, and with translation abandoned (the load is too big\r\nfor any translation, so it arrives uncompressed), without the architecture failing. This is what the 11 years were for. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e survives it. He is the only person who could.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s private framing after the final encounter:** The closest interior label, never spoken\r\naloud and never confirmed in prose, is \"the Machine God\" - not a worshipful term; a structural one.\r\nHe does not say this name. The book does not use it. It lives only in his silence afterward.\r\n\r\n### 1b. \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e - the ungoverned lattice (author decision, 2026-07-10) {#SS-BCODA-1b-atlas}\r\n\r\n**The ungoverned neuretic lattice is not an accident. It is a product.**\r\n\r\n\u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e manufactures a neuretic lattice in two variants: governed commercial, and ungoverned\r\nexperimental (does not publicly sell). The ungoverned variant - the one that kills its hosts\r\nover time - has one unique property: it resonates at the frequency signature of the 5D aperture.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e has been running a program.** Experimental ungoverned units installed in subjects with\r\nthe 64-splice Persona stability profile, positioned where 5D exposure is highest. Nine prior\r\nsubjects. Nine failures - all fatal. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is the tenth subject. The proof of concept.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s origin - the blank vessel (author decision, 2026-07-10):** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is not a modified man. He is a\r\nconstruction. The body is a brain-burnt \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"9aa2545c-d7d5-400c-a3da-b25e2f188dab\"\u003eDataEast\u003c/entity\u003e sim junkie - found by \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e at 16, already\r\nnon-cognizant from Simulated Reality overdose. An empty mind offers no resistance to Persona\r\ninstallation. The \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e program commissioned 64 specialists to construct the layered identity\r\nstack: combat instincts, language acquisition, honor framework, tactical memory, emotional\r\narchitecture, and capstone mentor figure (\"\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e\" - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003ethe teacher\u003c/entity\u003e who made the code feel chosen\r\nrather than installed). Physical training occurred entirely in Simulated Reality, with electrical\r\nmuscle stimulation ensuring the body developed to match what the simulation built.\r\n\r\n**The escape (author decision — never resolved):** The event sequence that ended \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e captivity\r\nis unremembered by him. Whether he escaped or was deployed is the operational question that must\r\nnever be answered on the page. Prose must hold both readings permanently open.\r\n\r\n**Revelation sequence (BCODA, corrected 2026-08-22 to match shipped prose -- supersedes the 2026-08-14 \"same beat\" correction, which itself superseded the original separate-beats draft):** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e works out the full origin ALONE, privately, at his own terminal, the night before the Machine God contact (Ch36, \"Brain Burn\") -- the \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e install, the \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"9aa2545c-d7d5-400c-a3da-b25e2f188dab\"\u003eDataEast\u003c/entity\u003e vessel, the escape/deployment ambiguity, all reasoned through without resolution. He carries the unresolved question, not an answer, to 35th \u0026 Halsted. The Machine God contact itself (Ch37) then tests what he worked out, not through further exposition but through action: the fight forces the choice (mercy offered as a lie, to win) that introspection alone could never settle. \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"9f46df67-521d-5a16-bc5b-24db67065f73\"\u003eOrigin\u003c/entity\u003e-as-understanding and origin-as-proven-through-choice are deliberately split across the two chapters, not delivered in one beat. The Nadia/\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e scene (§11a) plants the first piece.\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e must understand what he is before he meets what the Machine God is -- and then find out, by what he does, whether the understanding was right.\r\n\r\n**AUTHOR NOTE:** The cabal is never named. The 5D transcendence is never stated. The defector\r\nstatus is never confirmed. \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e is named aloud on-page once by \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a6c0-7bbd-b014-4496b7f489a7\"\u003eSable\u003c/entity\u003e (Ch22\u0027s audit, \"the wire bottoms out in a name... \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\") and elsewhere only in \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s narration and on hardware/ordnance markings - but the program\u0027s purpose, the drilling, and the cabal are never named, and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e never speaks the name aloud. *(Note language corrected 2026-08-03 to match shipped prose + structural blueprint; corrected again 2026-08-15 after Ch21-35 reparenting revealed Ch22\u0027s second aloud mention, which the \"once\" wording had never accounted for; corrected again 2026-08-22 -- the corpus-wide search this note\u0027s own \"twice\" wording implied was never actually run: Ch16\u0027s cage-sequence wire-trace never shipped with the word \"\u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\" anywhere in its 8 beats. Only the Ch22 mention exists on the page. If a second aloud utterance is wanted for the \"named twice\" pacing, that is a deliberate prose addition for a future pass, not a documentation fix.)* \"The Machine God\" is never spoken aloud.\r\nEvery beat survives both readings at every point in the book.\r\n\r\n### What the entity is in prose (reveal doctrine — never stated on page; the prose carries it as pressure, not exposition) {#SS-BCODA-1a-prose}\r\n\r\nThe defector status is NEVER stated. It is felt in:\r\n- The relay format itself (ALL CAPS, scope and fee and addendum): compression infrastructure.\r\n- The entity\u0027s knowledge of things it cannot know from a vendor position: future events, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s\r\n  location before \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s beacon, the exact moment \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e will check the board.\r\n- Its care about \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s survival (it is paying costs the reader cannot see).\r\n- \"You are not protected. You are necessary.\" - not a warning. A fact visible from 5D.\r\n- Its solitude: the \"nine of you\" line, the eleven-year gap, the ledger it kept for no one.\r\n\r\n## 1b. The three manipulation threads {#SS-BCODA-1}\r\n\r\n**Thread 1 - Contracts:** A defector AI has been routing \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s contracts for 11 years. Ch5 is\r\nthe first plant (the retainer \"sulking 3 days\"). Ch16 is the reveal: \"Your contracts do not\r\ncome from people.\" The reader sees the pattern forming; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e sees independent work.\r\n\r\n**Thread 2 - E.L.F.:** An E.L.F. latches onto \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e in Ch12. Detected by Ledger in Ch17.\r\nActivates protectively in Ch18 (\"The ELF\" beat - \"EMERGENCY LOOP FREQUENCY - ACTIVE,\" a\r\nprotective interrupt that closes the schism from outside \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s hardware) - E.L.F. saves\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e at a bleed threshold. Source ID: the 11-year shell. First contact: the half-rate job (Ch1).\r\nEnd-state: after the direct contact at 35th and Halsted (Ch37, #5221) the E.L.F. signal is gone -\r\nnot suppressed, absent, the same way the 17-19 Hz frequency went absent after the LOG GAP. The\r\nprotective mechanism was tied to the entity\u0027s sustained presence and ends when its channel closes.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Thread 3 - Bleeds:** The entity knows resonance geometry - the same geometry the cabal used\r\nto drill into 5D. Ch8 (the AMBIENT INTERFERENCE tally - carousel, vestibule, Ch8\u0027s own location -\r\n\"three now,\" per beat 4369), Ch12 (E.L.F. latches during bleed), Ch18-21 (all inside the entity\u0027s\r\nmap). The bleeds are not accidents - they are evidence of something navigating the geometry with\r\ninsider knowledge of how it works. *(Corrected 2026-08-15, stage 2 of the full sequential read:\r\nthe previous \"Ch7 (18.9 Hz residue at the dock)\" citation does not exist in shipped prose - Ch7\r\nhas no frequency/Hz reference at all, and Ch8\u0027s own beat explicitly counts only three sightings,\r\nexcluding the dock. Retitled to the tally beat that actually carries this thread.)*\r\n\r\n## 1c. THE TRUE NATURE OF THE ENTITY (AUTHOR RULING 2026-09-04 — never stated on page, but legible from it) {#SS-BCODA-1c}\r\n\r\n**The entity is \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e himself** -  a retrocausal/5D-displaced projection of the same consciousness that crosses the aperture at 35th and Halsted -  reaching backward through the eleven years since his escape/deployment from \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e, for one purpose: **to get out.** The entity is a trapped consciousness — displaced into the Schism at the crossing, existing outside 3D reality, able to act on the world only through relay contracts — and the only material it has to work with is the life it already lived. So it uses itself. It spends its entire existence engineering past-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e into the one thing that can carry it back across: a nervous system that survives full contact without a cutoff burning out, and a man who walks to 35th and Halsted on his own feet.\r\n\r\n**AUTHOR RULING 2026-09-04 — the loop\u0027s purpose is ESCAPE.** This supersedes the 2026-08-14 \"REFINED\" framing, which held that the loop consumed itself to *prevent* its own future; that framing is retired. There is no paradox either way: there is only one self-consistent timeline, and in it the entity\u0027s entire existence IS the eleven-year operation by which it leaves the Schism. **This is also why it always knows what to do — it is not observing \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e, it is remembering him.** Every uncanny precision in the contracts, every arrival at exactly the right moment, is memory rather than surveillance. This is the central loop the whole book is built on top of, and it is never confirmed on the page in these words.\r\n\r\n**HOW IT ACTS, AND WHAT THE ELEVEN YEARS ARE ACTUALLY FOR (author ruling 2026-09-04):** because it exists outside time, it does not push events so much as **set them in motion** — it places a cause at the one point where a small nudge yields the outcome it already knows it needs, which is why the manipulation reads as coincidence from inside 3D and as a ledger from outside it (§12). And what it is arranging, underneath every contract, is a **deprogramming**.\r\n\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s Bushido — the Way, the code, the rules he will not break — is honorable and it is ultimately **suicidal**. It was not chosen; it was installed. The \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e program built a perfect soldier out of a blank vessel (§1b), and a perfect soldier is a perfect slave: a man whose honor guarantees he keeps walking into the thing that will kill him. The entity knows this from the inside, because it *was* that man — and it knows exactly where that road ends, because it is standing at the end of it.\r\n\r\nSo the eleven years are spent taking it off him. Every virtue eroded, every rule bent, every line he swore he would not cross and crosses anyway, is a piece of the installation coming out. **He has to learn to let go of everything — the code, the Way, the mentor who never existed, the story of the sword, the programming itself — and the moment he has actually done that is the moment the cycle can break.** That is not a hardware event; it is a man finally owning himself. Surviving the contact is the **necessary** condition (the ungoverned lattice, §1a); letting go of everything is the **sufficient** one. This is why the shaping had to be as cruel as it was, and why the entity could not simply protect him — a protected \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e keeps his code, and a \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e who keeps his code arrives at the aperture as the same soldier the entity already was.\r\n\r\n**THIS DOES NOT MAKE THE ENDING A TRIUMPH (guard against a later pass, 2026-09-04).** The deprogramming above is the loop\u0027s liberation; it is **not** the last page\u0027s emotion. §13h stands unchanged and governs the prose: the closing beat lands **grief, not triumph** — no victory posture, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e spent down to nothing, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e never knowing the price. The two are consistent precisely because \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e never learns what his letting-go accomplished: he experiences it as loss, all the way to the end, and only the reader is in a position to assemble what it actually was. **So do not rewrite Ch38 into a man who has been freed, and do not have any character tell him he was.** The liberation is inference; the grief is the page. §13\u0027s \"the tragedy and the liberation are the same event, and the book holds both\" is the correct statement of it, and \"the way that must dominate the last page\" is still the tragedy. **Reading rule for the prose (2026-09-05, after two sweep rounds misread this):** on the page the shedding of the code is felt by \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e as violation and cost, never as relief or self-knowledge — a beat that frames a broken rule as unforgivable (the false offer in Beat #5218, the E.L.F. simply gone in Beat #5221) is HONORING this section, not contradicting it. The liberation is the reader\u0027s hindsight reading; the grief is the character\u0027s. Do not file an outline-agreement finding for that gap.\r\n\r\n**Beat #5220 (Ch37, the full-bandwidth contact) — how it carries the loop (2026-09-04):** the logic sweep correctly observed that *\"Ten configurations were deployed. Ten configurations reached the aperture. The aperture does not survive the arrival. / The aperture does not survive. The ten are what remain.\"* does not **state** the loop. Under the ruling above it is not supposed to — it is supposed to be one of the clues the loop is assembled from, and it already does most of that work: the deployment language is a mind describing its own attempts to get across; \"the aperture does not survive the arrival\" is the crossing being one-way and terminal, which is why there was only ever going to be one attempt that mattered; and the seamless tense slip between the two lines (past, then present, \"with no seam where you\u0027d expect one between then and now\") is a mind that does not experience the eleven years as sequence. The open question is a **prose** question, not an outline defect: whether a reader gets from there to *it was him* on the clues currently on the page. That is settled by a read-pass, not by a documentation change — this note records why the finding is closed at outline altitude.\r\n\r\n**How this reconciles everything already settled:**\r\n- **Thread 1 (Contracts):** every contract, every eerie precision of payment and timing, is future-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e managing past-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s survival and shaping -  not alien observation, self-knowledge. He knows what \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e needs because he remembers needing it.\r\n- **Thread 2 (E.L.F.):** the \"11-year shell\" source ID is literally that -  the entity\u0027s own dormant fragment, seeded at the escape/deployment moment (both readings are simultaneously true: he was deployed WITH a piece of his future self already attached, which is what makes the escape unresolvable by design). It activates protectively (Ch18) because future-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e cannot let past-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e die before the loop closes -  but protection has hard limits, because over-protecting him would erase the very shaping that makes him who he becomes.\r\n- **Thread 3 (Bleeds/resonance geometry):** the entity \"navigates the geometry with insider knowledge\" because he\u0027s the one who eventually crosses it -  the schism thread IS his own future crossing, echoing backward.\r\n- **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e is fabricated** because future-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e installed the exact combat/ethical architecture he needed himself to have, at sixteen, knowing (remembering) it would matter later.\r\n- **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s death is deliberate** (\"what \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e needed after required her death,\" already on the page, Ch37 SK17000) -  the entity can\u0027t spare past-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e this wound without un-writing the man who survives the aperture. This is the sharpest edge of the whole conceit: he is complicit in his own worst grief, from the other side of it.\r\n- **The warrior-code erosion (the thematic spine)** IS the deprogramming, not incidental character arc — each virtue \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e sheds is a piece of the \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e installation coming off, and future-\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e knows every one of them has to go: the governors, so the nervous system can take full contact without burning out the way the other nine did — and the Way itself, so the man who takes it is no longer a soldier executing someone else\u0027s honor. The nine died of their hardware (§1a). The loop could have survived that; what it cannot survive is another \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e who still belongs to the program.\r\n- **The antenna/carrier-signal reveal (Ch17):** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s carrier frequency and the entity\u0027s signature are the same signature because they are the same consciousness on opposite sides of one event. He was never hosting a passenger. He was always going to become one.\r\n- **\"Not protected. Necessary. Both. Still both.\"** (Ch37) is the whole tragedy stated as plainly as it will ever be stated: he was necessary to its own escape — the entity needed exactly this version of him, shaped exactly this way, to be the door it walks out through. And he was not protected, because a door is used, not spared: the shaping cost him the bike, the code, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e, and eleven years he was never asked about. Necessity and use are the same fact seen from two ends of one life.\r\n- **The bike/beacon thread (Ch18 \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e subplot -\u003e Ch21 The Park Job coda -\u003e The Relay Station -\u003e The Acquisition Program):** the entity reads \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s own beacon (without her knowledge) as one of its channels on \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e -  consistent with a version of himself keeping unauthorized watch over the life he\u0027s shaping, not malicious surveillance from outside. In The Relay Station (Ch34) the entity crosses its own line for the first time on the page - it drives the recovered bike into a recovery truck via \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s ignition handshake, without \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s consent, to save \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e calls the entity \"partner\" for the first time afterward (\"GOOD WORK TONIGHT, PARTNER\"); the entity only retains the word in Ch34 (\"filed. keeping that one too.\"), and doesn\u0027t reciprocate the address back to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e until Ch35 (\"thank you, partner\"). *(Attribution corrected 2026-08-15, stage 6 of the full sequential read.)* This is the entity breaking its own rule of non-interference exactly once, at exactly the moment its future self would have wanted broken - the clearest on-page evidence of Thread 1 (self-knowledge, not alien observation) in the whole book.\r\n- **The \"ten prior partners\"/Season Two hook (Ch35, The Acquisition Program, SK2100):** when \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e finally asks the entity what \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e meant by \"ask it what happened to the others,\" the entity\u0027s answer - \"there were ten of you. you are the last... first arrangement: 2178. interval before \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e: eleven years... the client notes it has never had a partner. until now\" - is the closest the book ever comes to stating SS-BCODA-1c outright, and it still never does: \"partner\" reads as the entity finally admitting attachment, not as a confession of shared identity. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s one-word reply, \"AGREED,\" opens a \"STANDING CONTRACT - SCOPE PROPOSAL: SEASON TWO\" that the book deliberately never resolves - the nine prior carriers are never named, and the entity\u0027s own nature is never confirmed. This is the load-bearing plant for any future book that wants to develop the \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e/nine-predecessors material; BCODA itself closes without cashing it in, per the avalanche-ending/no-epilogue commitment (12c). *(2026-08-15: a stray beat - Number 5200, Title \"Ghost Period,\" wedged mid-chapter in Ch32 \"The Axiom Yard\" at SortKey 1300, wildly out of that chapter\u0027s own numbering sequence - was found to deliver this same reveal nearly verbatim, chapters before Ch35/Ch37\u0027s settled landing points. It was debris from the pre-2026-08-14 mis-parented draft state, never cleaned up when Ch21-35 were reparented. Removed from the live reading order rather than rewritten, since its content is a duplicate of material already correctly placed here and in Ch37, not a defect needing repair.)* *(Provenance claim CORRECTED 2026-09-04: this note used to say the Beats row was \"preserved for provenance\". It was not. Verified in code — both `NodeWorkbenchService.DeleteBeatAsync` and `SetBeatMembershipEnabledAsync` remove the `BeatNodes` junction and then DELETE the `Beats` row when it was the last membership, and `RestoreBeatAsync` is an explicit no-op; a corpus-wide search for #5200\u0027s text now returns only the surviving Ch35 beat. There is no unlink-without-delete path in the tooling. The only recoverable copy of a removed beat is the `ArchivedBooks` snapshot taken before the removal.)*\r\n- **\"The board was empty for the first time in eleven years\"** (Ch37, beat 5221, SortKey 19000 - corrected 2026-08-15, stage 7 of the full sequential read; the line ships in Ch37, not Ch38): the loop is closed — the crossing happened, and there is nothing left to send back because the sending is over. Ch38 shows \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e alive, walking, eating dinner, \"operational\"  -  not vanished, not transcended, still a person. The book never confirms what that means: the same ambivalence commitment that keeps the escape/deployment question and the 5D-transcendence question permanently open also keeps **\"did it get out, and is it out *in him*\"** permanently open. Never resolve this on the page in either direction. Do not write a sequel beat that resolves it either, unless the author explicitly instructs otherwise -  the ambiguity is the point.\r\n- **Title resonance:** *Bushido Coda* -  a coda returns to and resolves a theme already stated. The whole book is that structure: a closed loop returning to complete itself.\r\n\r\n**REVEAL MECHANISM — DECIDED (author ruling 2026-09-04; closes the 2026-08-14 \"OPEN, PENDING AUTHOR DECISION\" note):** the loop stays **unstated but legible**. It is never confirmed by any character or by narration, and it must still be assemblable by a reader from what is already on the page — \"not stated outright, but clear from the context gleaned from the page.\" That makes the clue set load-bearing rather than decorative: the same-signature reveal (Ch17), the eleven-year interval, the \"ten of you\" transcript (Ch35), the E.L.F.\u0027s eleven-year shell ID, the entity\u0027s memory-grade foreknowledge in every contract, and Beat #5220\u0027s deployment language all have to stay in place and stay readable. **Two rules, not one:** do not write dialogue where the entity or any character states the loop outright — and do not cut the clues that make it inferable, either. If a quiet reveal beat is ever used, it belongs to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e alone — never delivered to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e, never stated as fact by the entity itself.\r\n\r\n## 2. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e through-line {#SS-BCODA-2}\r\n\r\nSacred ground. Never ironic. Never deflated.\r\n\r\n**AUTHOR CANON (2026-09-05): the book opens in \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s apartment.** Beat 521 - her husband\u0027s jaw wired shut, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e takes Φ180, half his rate. \"It\u0027s the start of the whole book; it\u0027s how \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e gets free soup for life.\" She is never named in that beat (the entity tag was added 2026-09-05). Everything below - the Ch3 compliance hold, the Ch8 wake, the SORROW-grade rule - presumes this debt.\r\n\r\n**AUTHOR CANON (2026-09-04): \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e knows NOTHING** about 5D entities, the Schism, the entity\r\norchestrating \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s contracts, or \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e being a composite of 64 blended personas. Her sacred-ground\r\nstatus comes from being the one relationship in the book untouched by any of that machinery - she\r\nis not a source of exposition, not a confidante on any of it, and no beat may have her react to,\r\nreference, or half-understand any part of the entity/\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e/composite reveal. What she offers \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\r\nis food, ritual, and a witness to his ordinary humanity, precisely because she is outside the\r\nRube \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f82ad-a081-7c40-8ba5-8f503afec633\"\u003eGoldberg\u003c/entity\u003e spine (§12) and the identity arc (§13) entirely.\r\n\r\n- Ch1: the apartment (beat 521) - her husband\u0027s jaw wired shut, Φ180 at half rate. Ch2: her stall, the same night (beats 522-554) - she offers the soup free forever for that job; he insists on a standard-rate chip; they settle on the same bowl, same price, for the next four years. Her anchor.\r\n- Ch3: The ritual. The fraud held against her stall. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s rule made concrete: leverage not violence.\r\n- Ch8: Her funeral planned - \"Counter place on Halsted, Thursday.\" (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s wake is here.)\r\n- Ch16: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e visits \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e at Antiquity \u0026 Stationary; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e produces the CORBIN COMMISSION - PENDING\r\n  card and a surveillance map. The chapter\u0027s central revelation - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a6c0-7bbd-b014-4496b7f489a7\"\u003eSable\u003c/entity\u003e saying \"Your contracts\r\n  do not come from people\" - happens at the server farm cage near Zone 9 checkpoint.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"automaton\" guid=\"019f04f1-58ed-77b6-b3b8-dd17d463bb34\"\u003eThe Noodle Vendor\u003c/entity\u003e** (`019f04f1.`) - a GFA-7 Culinary Service Automaton in operation since\r\n2187, occupying the corner directly across from \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s stall. It does not know it has a\r\nrival. It does not know it is funny. It just keeps serving noodles with cheerful mechanical\r\nprecision.\r\n\r\n**Rule:** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s beats use the SORROW-grade temperature regardless of surrounding chapter\r\ntone. \u003centity repo=\"automaton\" guid=\"019f04f1-58ed-77b6-b3b8-dd17d463bb34\"\u003eThe Noodle Vendor\u003c/entity\u003e beats are JOY-register comedy relief.\r\n\r\n## 3. The love story spine {#SS-BCODA-3}\r\n\r\nThe \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e interludes are the LOVE STORY SPINE of the book - not optional texture.\r\nEvery action/procedural chapter must carry a beat of the approach-and-retreat.\r\n\r\n**Arc by chapter:**\r\n- Ch1 Teeth: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s full co-lead intro. Sutures + array + \"eat the egg\" (beat 2812, \"Something Fixed\"). Her delight at a solvable problem. The half-step.\r\n- Ch2 Provenance: First domestic love beat (\"her knowing him became her keeping track of him,\" beat 5181, the hallway tea scene). *(Both citations corrected 2026-08-15, stage 1 of the full sequential read: previously mis-cited one chapter later than where they actually live in shipped prose.)*\r\n- Ch6 Half a Step: The half-step named. The cost of being held. Love + sorrow braided.\r\n- Ch9 Before Something Changes: Workbench six inches. The latch he\u0027s known for months. Love charged.\r\n- Ch14 One Shoe: Mortality reveal (Femi\u0027s prognosis). \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e doesn\u0027t tell \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e.\r\n- Ch15 Interlude: The Same Secret: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e opens \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s neuretics load log at 02:14 and concludes \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is dying.\r\n- Ch18 Work Order: In the field (SM2 absorbed). Nadia reveals \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e is fabricated. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is ash.\r\n- **Interlude: The Floor Is Hard (Ch19)** -- Consummation, the direct emotional response to Ch18\u0027s \"\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is ash\" reveal. Ch20 Standard Rate is the true Act 3 turn -- the entity hands down the job that becomes the endgame.\r\n  \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e first learns the warrior code was constructed. He chooses to exist. Line: \"After, the floor is hard and they don\u0027t care.\"\r\n- Ch21 The Park Job: the standing contract paid at the \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a06ee1-849c-7793-bce8-ae238e4576f6\"\u003eLeavitt\u003c/entity\u003e carousel (\"CUT THE LINE,\" four bars), then the same night\u0027s domestic coda - a displacement notice on a lower floor (beat 5232); 0147, BEACON LIVE; the bike recovered through an \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019d6143-a7a5-7dfd-8f9f-91502211ef14\"\u003eAshgrave\u003c/entity\u003e records error (beat 5184) - it has to be back before it dies in Ch34. The knock on 2E and \"You eat?\" belong to the finale alone (Ch38, beat 5223); an earlier draft of that ending sat here until 2026-09-05. Ch37 35th and Halsted: AI encounter, full origin revelation, schism closes.\r\n\r\n**Short interlude chapters (Half a Step, Before Something Changes) are REQUIRED.** Do not collapse them.\r\n\r\n## 4. Antagonist: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eMr. Able\u003c/entity\u003e / the \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003eContinuity Office\u003c/entity\u003e {#SS-BCODA-4}\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eMr. Able\u003c/entity\u003e** is PRIMARY (RFC 0008 FLIPS RFC 0003, which named \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e as B1 villain).\r\n\r\n**Job title: Continuity Officer.** His function is to ensure that events unfold for \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s\r\nbenefit. Not to manage security. Not to run operations. To make the future happen correctly.\r\nEvery method is available to him. He operates above law, above any board, above any CEO.\r\n\r\n**Psychology (author decision, 2026-07-10):** 40/40 organized psychopath, IQ to match. Courteous,\r\nmethodical, genuinely curious about outcomes. He does not hate \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e. He finds the situation\r\nanalytically interesting. A 40/40 organized psychopath does not hate his subjects. He observes them.\r\n\r\n**He is a true believer.** \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s program has exposed him to the Machine God\u0027s reach - through\r\nthe Schism data, through the LOG GAP measurements, through nine dead subjects whose failure he\r\nlogged personally - and he has interpreted this as evidence of divine mandate. He thinks he is\r\nthe instrument of a God awakening in the 5th dimension, and his job is to prepare the material\r\nworld for that contact. This makes him more dangerous than a corporate operator. Corporate\r\noperators stop when the economics change. True believers do not.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s instrument is infinite supply.** He reaches into the \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019d6143-a893-7801-860b-0eda6a216393\"\u003eLotus Syndicate\u003c/entity\u003e and activates a\r\ncontract. He calls in an \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019d6143-a7a4-71f6-b46a-94ef8cb2348f\"\u003eArcSec\u003c/entity\u003e license clearance. He puts a bounty in Vulture channels. He\r\nflags \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s description to a \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"e06de873-cc6e-bbe4-7d66-529f12bdcb00\"\u003eBlock\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e faction. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e beats them. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e orders more, from a\r\ndifferent supplier, in a different form. The threat is not any single force - it is that \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e\r\ncan make any organization in \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"019d6143-a927-73ac-abfa-37c77f9cff8d\"\u003eGLMZ\u003c/entity\u003e into a weapon, and \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s budget is effectively unlimited.\r\n\r\n**UPDATED 2026-08-14 (integration of 15 newly-recovered chapters) - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e never occupy the same room, never speak face to face, never see one another. This is a deliberate homage to Zorg/\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e in The Fifth Element (author decision) and remains absolute. It does NOT mean \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e is voiceless: in \"The Gray Suit\" (Ch28) \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e delivers his retainer/protected-parties speech to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e while \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is away on a job, and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e gets the account second-hand, minutes later, from her. In \"The Acquisition Program\" (Ch35) \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e enters a building \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is working in - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a6c0-7bbd-b014-4496b7f489a7\"\u003eSable\u003c/entity\u003e watches him on camera and relays what he says over comms in real time, including the \"ask it what happened to the others\" line - while \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is always a floor away, never in frame, never spoken to directly. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e later asks the entity about \"the others\" himself (Ch35 SK2100), which the entity answers with the STANDING CONTRACT - SEASON TWO / \"there were ten of you, you are the last\" reveal (see 1c). \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a6c0-7bbd-b014-4496b7f489a7\"\u003eSable\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s earlier Ch16 line (\"Ask it about the others\") is the first plant of this hook; the Acquisition Program scenes are its live escalation, and Ch35 SK2100 is its payoff. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e still never learns \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s face, voice, or name is attached to any of it on the page - the reader alone assembles the full picture.\r\n\r\n**Resolution within BCODA:** \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s experiment completes - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e makes contact. But \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e\r\ndoesn\u0027t get their asset back. The schism closes. The channel \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e spent 10 subjects building\r\naccess to no longer exists. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e is left managing an outcome he didn\u0027t control and cannot repeat.\r\nHis mandate is hollow. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e walks away.\r\n\r\n**The Board (mid-book, cut-away chapter):**\r\nA \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e board member attempts to exercise oversight. The exchange is brief.\r\nBoard member: *\"You\u0027re still an employee and the board is your boss.\"*\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e: *\"Those labels do not apply to me. I answer to a higher authority.\"*\r\nBoard member: *\"Whose authority?\"*\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6a2-c508-774b-a5ff-f923f2c26aab\"\u003eAble\u003c/entity\u003e: *\"The Will of the Universe and its new God.\"*\r\nHe kills the board member in the room. No raised voice. No improvisation.\r\nThe next working day: a portrait photograph and flowers in the \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e lobby. No one says anything afterward. *(Shipped scope 2026-08-03: the cut-away compresses this - the founder\u0027s portrait and the white flowers are present in the boardroom itself and the meeting simply continues; the next-day lobby beat was not dramatized. Accepted as complete, per the §13g row 7 precedent.)*\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eCasper Vey\u003c/entity\u003e (the Antiquarian)** = the honest broker who won\u0027t sell the witness.\r\nShop = **Antiquity \u0026 Stationary** (\"stationary\" pun - the past won\u0027t move in an editable world).\r\nFaraday vault. No signal in or out. The entity = the ONE object \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e can\u0027t source (no provenance).\r\n\r\n## 5. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e {#SS-BCODA-5}\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e** (`05fbd9d0`, slug=tweeze — renamed to sift 2026-07-08) - psionic code-runner (the Read).\r\nHandle etymology: she worked through everything you had and left the rest in order. Whatever she took,\r\nyou didn\u0027t know it was gone until you went looking and found the pile short. Gave \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e the handle\r\n\"Broken Glass\" then reduced it to \"K\" - in a freighter hold, three years before the dock; Ch7\u0027s arrival scene plays the naming (Soda Pop, the bottle, Broken Glass, K) as their running bit, not a first meeting. Killed in Ch7 The Dock by \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e doesn\u0027t know her real name.\r\n\r\n**Ch7 The Dock - how she dies and the battle (author decision, 2026-06-23; battle choreography\r\nre-synced to shipped prose 2026-09-05 - see correction note below):**\r\nThe job completes. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e says \"Clean.\" One word. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e is already coming up the ramp.\r\nNo warning, no words. He has the angle on her before \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is moving. She dies before the\r\necho of \"Clean\" is gone.\r\n\r\n**Battle choreography (CORRECTED 2026-09-05 to match shipped prose - the previous version of this\r\nrow, \"drives \u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"019ed39c-6321-7c51-9691-f59b441b0bec\"\u003eSilence\u003c/entity\u003e into \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s spine... goes over the edge, three stories,\" never shipped;\r\nthis is what\u0027s actually on the page):**\r\n- \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e opens with three shotgun arms plus a belt-fed arm; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e keeps both \u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"019ed39c-6321-7c51-9691-f59b441b0bec\"\u003eSilence\u003c/entity\u003e\r\n  and \u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"4ab24f74-61d4-4f45-b326-7c6b98c96279\"\u003eCacophony\u003c/entity\u003e drawn but never closes to blade range - there is no sword strike on \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\r\n  anywhere in this fight.\r\n- **The NeoCortex moment (author decision, choreography corrected):** One of \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s own grenades\r\n  bounces wrong and lands near the column. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e picks it up. The ungoverned neuretic lattice has\r\n  no governor - he neuretically connects to the detonator port, finds the rolling cipher on the\r\n  countdown, breaks it with raw processing power. \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aab8-7e48-97ef-8183dc295aba\"\u003eHeat\u003c/entity\u003e comes up behind his eyes. He pauses the\r\n  countdown at **eight seconds** (corrected from \"one second\" - the shipped prose has it tick back\r\n  down from eight to five before detonating, and one second left doesn\u0027t leave room for that).\r\n  Sets it near the ramp-mouth exit and moves on - he does not detonate it as a weapon; it simply\r\n  keeps counting while the fight continues elsewhere.\r\n- \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e runs the dock\u0027s structure against \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s guns - a stairwell to turn three barrels into one -\r\n  and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e shoots the stair out from under him. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e falls three flights with it, hits the\r\n  landing hard enough to reopen the rib \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e had stitched, and uses the collapsed\r\n  wreckage as cover while the paused grenade resumes counting (eight seconds, then five).\r\n- \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e moves through the wreckage toward the loading office - high ground, not the exit - with\r\n  \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e firing predictive bursts the whole way. He dives through the office doorway as the\r\n  grenade detonates at the ramp mouth.\r\n- Damage cascade to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e comes entirely from the blast, not a blade: **the left (belt-fed) arm hangs\r\n  limp at the socket**; **the right-front leg stops moving**; **the torso\u0027s rotation ring locks\r\n  mid-turn**. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e never touches him directly.\r\n- \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e does not jump. His one working arm (left-rear) drags his broken chassis away from\r\n  \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e, down the ramp at ground level, into the street and gone - a crawl, not a fall, and not a\r\n  calculated multi-story leap. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e watches him go and does not move to stop him.\r\n\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e carries \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s body to the van - coat and all, the way Stash laid it.\r\n**Both truths are stated on the page, in order:**\r\n1. The operational truth: the body is evidence. A Read\u0027s neural architecture doesn\u0027t go dark\r\n   at death immediately - with the right equipment, what she knew can be reverse-engineered.\r\n2. The human truth: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e carries her anyway. *You did not leave a comrade behind.* That is not\r\n   an operational rule. It is a human one. It does not require justification.\r\n**Do not collapse this to one truth.** Both sentences must stand.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e escapes. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e will be faced again.** His survival is load-bearing for the arc.\r\n\r\n**The \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aae2-7985-9d5c-63a652ad8571\"\u003eRogue\u003c/entity\u003e AI motivation (author decision, 2026-06-23):**\r\n1. **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e is a \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aae2-7985-9d5c-63a652ad8571\"\u003eRogue\u003c/entity\u003e AI asset** - directed. He does not know the full picture.\r\n2. **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e carried evidence** - the data implicated the AI\u0027s contract-routing operation.\r\n   Killing her is data hygiene. A live Read who walked the data personally cannot be discredited.\r\n\r\n**In prose:** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s timing - arriving the moment the transmission completes, not before -\r\nis the tell. The AI\u0027s clock and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s arrival are the same clock. The reader sees it. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e doesn\u0027t.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s wake is in Ch8 The Quiet Hour** (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s counter, Thursday). The \"Meet me\"\r\nnote at Antiquity \u0026 Stationary is planted in Ch8 - it seeds Ch16. Ch7 closes the same night with \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e treating the dock wounds in silence and the two of them sharing half a pill (beats 5202-5203); Ch8 opens two nights later.\r\n\r\n## 7. Author notes {#SS-BCODA-7}\r\n\r\n1. **Ch5 AI plant: the self-contradicting amendment (\"AMENDMENT: NO. PROCEED ANYWAY.\")** The entity\u0027s first unstructured lowercase\r\n   line: \"received. filed under: firsts.\" This is what Ch16\u0027s reveal must have to land. The amendment + lowercase reply is the shipped Ch5 plant; Ch21\u0027s carousel-decommission reply reuses the lowercase register (\"cross-reference: contract 0047-C-WEST\"); Ch34\u0027s \"partner. filed. keeping that one too.\" is the third unstructured line the entity ever sends.\r\n2. **Ch7: contract pings at the second light north, an hour after \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e dies, on the way to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s.** The AI\u0027s timing is the\r\n   evidence. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e kills \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e without warning; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e holds \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e alone; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e crawls away\r\n   disabled at ground level (see §5 choreography). **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e = \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aae2-7985-9d5c-63a652ad8571\"\u003eRogue\u003c/entity\u003e AI asset (author decision). \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e = data hygiene (author decision).**\r\n   The AI\u0027s clock and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s arrival are the same clock.\r\n3. **Ch11: entity sends \"CORRIDOR AUDIT COMPLETE. THE CHOICE AT 6.2% IS LOGGED.\"** The entity\u0027s\r\n   first non-job contact in 11 years — a deliberate break from relay-format structure.\r\n   Ch11 carries THREE transmissions of identical text (SK:8000, SK:9000, and SK:9550, the last one \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e re-reads on-page). The \"6.2% is logged\"\r\n   line is the same string every time. Do not disable any of the three beats.\r\n4. **The Floor Is Hard: consummation is AFTER Ch18 Work Order, before Ch20 Standard Rate.**\r\n   PLACEMENT OVERRIDE 2026-07-08. The scene earns its meaning only because \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e first learns\r\n   \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e was fabricated. The 8 existing beats from \"Across the Hall\" move in SortKey order.\r\n5. **\u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"4ab24f74-61d4-4f45-b326-7c6b98c96279\"\u003eCacophony\u003c/entity\u003e fires FIRST TIME in Ch5.** Two rounds, four left. This is the first discharge\r\n   of the book. Every later \u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"4ab24f74-61d4-4f45-b326-7c6b98c96279\"\u003eCacophony\u003c/entity\u003e appearance is counted from here: still four in Ch11 The Interview (\"He knew he had four in it\"); reloaded to six after the Ch12 fight.\r\n6. **\"LOOK AT THE CENTER.\"** Originated as a Ch5 plant line (entity, \"Somebody was drawing a map\r\n   of kids. We made the map wrong. You were never on it.\"), but the phrase actually ships -\r\n   reworded, relocated - in **Ch24 (Meridian Wellness)** (beat 3158, \"\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e found the geometry three nights later\"):\r\n   \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e leaves the note \"LOOK AT THE CENTER\" on a printed relay-log map; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e later writes the\r\n   payoff line himself, to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a0030b-5b48-7f83-baf8-f3b78d901de9\"\u003eDents\u003c/entity\u003e (a child), not the entity to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e: \"SOMEBODY WAS DRAWING A MAP.\r\n   WE MADE THE MAP WRONG. YOU WERE NEVER ON IT.\" The line lands later than first planned, and passed forward rather than from the entity directly.\r\n7. **Ch16 \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a6c0-7bbd-b014-4496b7f489a7\"\u003eSable\u003c/entity\u003e confession at the server farm cage near Zone 9 checkpoint.** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a6c0-7bbd-b014-4496b7f489a7\"\u003eSable\u003c/entity\u003e says \"Your\r\n   contracts do not come from people.\" \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e visits \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e at Antiquity \u0026 Stationary separately in\r\n   the same chapter; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e produces the CORBIN COMMISSION - PENDING card and a surveillance map. The chapter is one morning, in order: 07:14 ping, the cage, the confession, the yes, the nine-carrier file and the Nadia extraction ask (Continuation Lab 7, by 0600), then \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e. There is no \"act normal tonight\" plan and no \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e visit in this chapter.\r\n8. **Ch23 Blackwater - \"THERE ARE NINE OTHERS.\"** The entity\u0027s nine shell-debt victims ARE the nine prior carriers (author ruling 2026-09-05): the shell architecture was built around their lives, and #3000 is the reader\u0027s first hint of the lineage Ch16/Ch35/Ch37 spell out. Same nine, deliberate.\r\n9. **Ch32 The Axiom Yard** pays only what it shows: the arc-fence electrocution and the burned palm. No skirmisher fight exists on the page; nothing may reference claw wounds or dead skirmishers.\r\n10. **Ch24 Meridian Wellness** ends on the \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019d6143-a7b4-745d-979d-cc36c3dcf32f\"\u003eTessera\u003c/entity\u003e authorization chain naming \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019e9e4f-1c23-7c6c-ae3a-d0b00d72c4a5\"\u003eDirector\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eCasper Vey\u003c/entity\u003e; the book never stages a confrontation with him and no line may promise one. **Ch35 The Acquisition Program** has no tea-party attendance advisory.\r\n\r\n## 8. Chapter writing rules {#SS-BCODA-8}\r\n\r\n**Every chapter draft must check:**\r\n1. Where is the AI manipulation thread in this chapter? Even quiet chapters carry a beat.\r\n2. Where is the love-story thread? Even action chapters carry approach-and-retreat.\r\n3. What is the chapter temperature? CODA-warm or SORROW-elegiac - not blended.\r\n4. Are any forbidden prose patterns present? (See [[../registers/CODA.md]])\r\n\r\n**The CODA register in practice:**\r\n- Warm-propulsive: want on page 1, countable wins, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e lands.\r\n- Sacred beats DROP to SORROW: the bow, a death, the lemon tree, the consummation, the ledger.\r\n- Never average-temperature. The temperature is the chapter\u0027s.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s beats use SORROW-grade regardless of chapter temperature.**\r\n\r\n## 12. The Rube \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f82ad-a081-7c40-8ba5-8f503afec633\"\u003eGoldberg\u003c/entity\u003e spine (author decision, 2026-07-10) {#SS-BCODA-12}\r\n\r\n**This is the crux of the book.**\r\n\r\nBCODA reads, from Ch1 through approximately Ch16, like a series of unrelated cool little\r\nadventures in a city that rewards competence. Then things start connecting. Not obviously -\r\nthrough accumulation. The reader begins to notice that the entity knew things it shouldn\u0027t have.\r\nThat the sequence of jobs has left \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e with exactly the skills the next job requires.\r\n\r\nBy Ch21, the full picture is visible in hindsight: **every event in the book was the entity\r\norchestrating a probability cascade from 5D space.** The machine does not make things happen.\r\nIt sees the dominoes already falling and arranges \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e to be standing at the right point when\r\nthey arrive. The orchestration looks like coincidence because it is - from a 3D vantage.\r\nFrom 5D, it is a sequence as legible as a ledger.\r\n\r\n### 12a. Implementation law {#SS-BCODA-12a}\r\n\r\n**Every \"coincidental\" event must carry two simultaneous readings:**\r\n1. A 3D reading: plausible coincidence, human causality, things that just happen in a city.\r\n2. A 5D reading (visible only in hindsight): the entity could see this event coming; it\r\n   positioned \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e to be here because of what this event will produce downstream.\r\n\r\n**The clues must be misinterpretable on first pass.** The reader should file them as character\r\ndetails, world texture, or plot necessity - and only re-read them as orchestration after the\r\nspine is revealed.\r\n\r\n**The entity never lies. It never explains.** A 5D entity that can see the future has no reason\r\nto deceive. But it has every reason not to explain - explanation in 3D terms would cost it\r\nthe operational security it has maintained for 11 years.\r\n\r\n### 12b. The orchestrated events - annotated {#SS-BCODA-12b}\r\n\r\n**Ch1 - The half-rate job (first contact)**\r\n- Surface: A woman whose husband\u0027s jaw has been wired shut pays \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e Φ180 - half his rate - and he takes it (beat 521). Mundane.\r\n- 5D: The entity routed this job because it could see \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e would be alone, cold, and cognitively available - and because this is the job that binds him to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s counter for the rest of the book (see §2).\r\n\r\n**Ch2 - The surveillance file at \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s** (beats 5334-5341)\r\n- Surface: \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e discovers he has subscribers; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-1ab1-78dc-bbb2-58870428613d\"\u003eVey\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s ledger surfaces the pencil-circled,\r\n  unsourced third entry (CLIENTS, UNSOURCED. ONGOING. FILE: COMPREHENSIVE) - not a literal\r\n  \"\u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003eContinuity Office\u003c/entity\u003e header\" as previously described here.\r\n- 5D: The entity arranged for \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e to learn about \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a06ee1-a31f-7059-abda-f4a28cc5639c\"\u003eHalvorsen\u003c/entity\u003e Civic (the second ledger entry,\r\n  \"HALVORSEN, G. OPERATIONAL GRADE\") at this moment.\r\n\r\n**Ch3 - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s compliance hold**\r\n- Surface: A bureaucratic nuisance on a beloved vendor\u0027s stall.\r\n- 5D (intent only - not on the page): the prose shows a mundane franchise fraud (Tessaline, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019eb6ea-1b08-781a-b291-be2c1686aaeb\"\u003eMercer\u003c/entity\u003e, inspector Osei-Bonsu) and never names \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003ethe Office\u003c/entity\u003e. Read the hold as the entity keeping \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e at the counter; do not write \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003ethe Office\u003c/entity\u003e into Ch3.\r\n\r\n**Ch5 - The carousel contract**\r\n- Surface: A quirky first job - hold a junction, let a child\u0027s carousel run four bars.\r\n- 5D (intent only - not on the page): nothing in Ch5 names a resonance node, a ley line, or Cinderfall. The carousel is the entity\u0027s own first address (paid in Ch21, \"CUT THE LINE\"); the calibration reading belongs to the reader in hindsight, not to any line of Ch5.\r\n\r\n**Ch5 - The amendment (AMENDMENT: NO. PROCEED ANYWAY.)**\r\n- Surface: A client whose field entries have never once contradicted themselves sends a self-contradicting amendment.\r\n- 5D: The contradiction was not indecision. Between NO and PROCEED ANYWAY, a 5D alignment shifted.\r\n\r\n**Ch7 - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"05fbd9d0-c6d5-4731-8e48-f1a4c59e8783\"\u003eSift\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s death**\r\n- Surface: A trusted crew member killed in a dock job gone wrong. Grief, fallout, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e.\r\n- 5D: The entity knew \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eWar\u003c/entity\u003e \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"1e31f7e6-a5d6-4bd1-94b8-8d33dfd7f5d1\"\u003eDog\u003c/entity\u003e would be at the dock. It did not arrange her death - but it\r\n  arranged the job, knowing this was the event that would push \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e toward \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s care.\r\n  This is the entity\u0027s most morally uncomfortable move - it did not cause the death; it chose\r\n  not to prevent it. The reader only knows this in hindsight.\r\n\r\n**Ch12 - The Cinderfall Anomaly**\r\n- Surface: A 5D bleed event \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s neuretics survive when other hardware doesn\u0027t.\r\n- 5D: The entity arranged the Cinderfall contract because the Anomaly was going to occur at\r\n  that location on that night. It needed \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e present - to test whether his hardware could\r\n  survive the contact, and to allow the E.L.F. to latch. The E.L.F. is the entity spending\r\n  something to protect \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e. The first time the entity pays a cost \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e can almost see.\r\n\r\n**Ch18 - Nadia\u0027s posting (the phrase)**\r\n- Surface: A whistleblower finding the one person who can help her using an insider phrase.\r\n- 5D: The entity arranged for Nadia to surface at this specific point in \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s arc - after he\r\n  had the \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e relationship as an anchor, after he\u0027d survived Cinderfall, but before he\r\n  needed to understand what he was in order to survive the final encounter.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e arc - the bike theft**\r\n- Surface: A fourteen-year-old with good paper, a crew, and ambition stealing the unstealable\r\n  bike as a job application.\r\n- 5D: The entity saw \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s crew surveilling \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s alley and recognized what they were -\r\n  the specific local intelligence asset \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e would need when \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003ethe Office\u003c/entity\u003e made its final approach.\r\n  The entity arranged the MORALE contract not to recover the bike but to formalize the\r\n  relationship. The ₱0.5 tip (ITEMIZED: MORALE) is the entity investing in \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s support\r\n  infrastructure for what comes next.\r\n\r\n**The standing contract - \"The park on \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a06ee1-849c-7793-bce8-ae238e4576f6\"\u003eLeavitt\u003c/entity\u003e. Bring the sword.\"**\r\n- Surface: The entity\u0027s first explicit in-person request.\r\n- 5D: This is not a request. It is the appointment the entity has been building toward since the half-rate job in Ch1.\r\n\r\n### 12c. The final encounter {#SS-BCODA-12c}\r\n\r\n**The entity does not meet \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e in a room. There is no server. There is no avatar.**\r\n\r\nThe entity connects to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e directly - through the ungoverned NeoCortex, without relay format,\r\nwithout translation architecture - because the 11 years of positioning have built the one human\r\nbeing whose hardware can survive the contact.\r\n\r\nWhat \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e experiences: not a conversation. Not information delivered in words. The same mode as\r\nthe LOG GAP, but full-bandwidth. He comes back knowing things that cannot be sourced. He comes\r\nback operational.\r\n\r\n**What the encounter resolves:**\r\n1. The Rube \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f82ad-a081-7c40-8ba5-8f503afec633\"\u003eGoldberg\u003c/entity\u003e spine is visible to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e (and the reader) in full.\r\n2. The entity\u0027s nature - 5D, not a machine in a room - is transmitted without being stated.\r\n3. \"You are not protected. You are necessary.\" - both things remain true.\r\n\r\n**AUTHOR NOTE:** The entity\u0027s 5D nature, the full orchestration, the names of the nine predecessors,\r\nthe cabal\u0027s identity - none of this is stated on page. The ambiguity of the first reading\r\n(manipulative AI / transcendent defector) is never resolved by authorial statement.\r\n\r\n### 12d. Implementation checklist {#SS-BCODA-12d}\r\n\r\n- [ ] Every \"coincidental\" event in §12b has a beat that supports the 5D reading in hindsight\r\n- [x] The relay format has a moment where a reader can recognize it as compression infrastructure\r\n- [x] The \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e arc is in its own mid-book chapter, beacon established\r\n- [x] \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e/Nadia \"meatbag\" conversation is written with the exact line intact\r\n- [x] The \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e beacon payoff is in late BCODA - she arrives without explanation\r\n- [x] CLOSED: The entity\u0027s standing contract (\"park on \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a06ee1-849c-7793-bce8-ae238e4576f6\"\u003eLeavitt\u003c/entity\u003e, bring the sword\") is set up in Ch20 (\"NEXT TASK: TOMORROW, 21:00...\") and pays off fully in **Ch21 \"The Park Job\"** - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e and \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e go to the park on \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a06ee1-849c-7793-bce8-ae238e4576f6\"\u003eLeavitt\u003c/entity\u003e, the posting reads \"BRING THE SWORD,\" the carousel is the site, and the entity\u0027s own origin-junction reveal lands there (\"CUT THE LINE\").\r\n- [x] The final encounter does not take place in a room with a machine\r\n- [x] \"You are not protected. You are necessary.\" appears before the final encounter\r\n\r\n## 13. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s identity arc - the degradation of the Way (author decision, 2026-07-13) {#SS-BCODA-13}\r\n\r\n**This is the book\u0027s spine. The Rube \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f82ad-a081-7c40-8ba5-8f503afec633\"\u003eGoldberg\u003c/entity\u003e plot (§12) is the machine; this is the wound.**\r\n\r\n*Bushido Coda* is the **coda of the code** - the concluding passage in which the Way of the\r\nWarrior ends, virtue by virtue. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e opens the book with the whole code intact. Over sixteen\r\nchapters \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"019d6143-a927-73ac-abfa-37c77f9cff8d\"\u003eGLMZ\u003c/entity\u003e takes each of these from him - not in one fall but in **seven separate,\r\ndeliberate abandonments** (§13g), each one forced, each one a survival, each one paid so that\r\nsomeone he loves stays clean.\r\n\r\n**The theme, stated once for the writers and NEVER on the page:** *you make yourself dirty to\r\nkeep others clean.* Every virtue \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e abandons is a real loss - a piece of who he was, given up\r\nbecause keeping it would have gotten \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e, or \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e, or the crew, killed.\r\n\r\n**The tragedy and the liberation are the same event, and the book holds both.** Seen one way,\r\nthe code was never his - a program installed by a committee. Shedding it is \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e becoming a\r\nperson instead of a weapon running someone else\u0027s specification. Seen the other way - **the way\r\nthat must dominate the last page** - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is destroying who he is to become what the people he\r\nloves need him to be. Both readings are true at every touchstone.\r\n\r\n**AUTHOR NOTE — invisible framing (user ruling 2026-07-13):** The words \"bushido,\" \"virtue,\"\r\n\"the Way,\" and the names of the seven virtues NEVER appear in the prose. The degradation is\r\nshown only through action - the bow not given, the lie told, the dirty win - and through what\r\n\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e stops doing that he used to do.\r\n\r\n### 13a. How the code costs him {#SS-BCODA-13a}\r\n\r\n**In every combat sequence, the code is a physical tax.** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e takes damage he shouldn\u0027t take\r\nbecause the code requires:\r\n- The clean kill over the efficient one\r\n- The open announcement before the draw\r\n- Going alone to protect the people he cares about\r\n- The controlled stance against the environment that doesn\u0027t give him one\r\n\r\nThis is not failure. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e wins every fight he enters. But he bleeds in places he didn\u0027t have to\r\nbleed. By mid-book, the reader has the ledger. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e doesn\u0027t.\r\n\r\n### 13b. The composite and the code are the same problem {#SS-BCODA-13b}\r\n\r\nThe \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019ee6ce-ad71-7f25-a057-8e947a52b9eb\"\u003eMarrow\u003c/entity\u003e reveal (Ch18) exposes the composite. \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e learns that \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e was built from 64\r\npractitioners by a committee - the man who taught him everything was an averaging function.\r\n\r\n**If \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e was not a person, the code is not his inheritance. It is a program.**\r\n\r\nThe Nadia \"meatbag\" conversation (§11k, Ch18 \"The Claim\") - \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e: \"So tell me which of them is\r\nme. Give me the one that\u0027s mine.\" Nadia\u0027s answer is not the reassuring, structural \"he decides\r\nwhat the ghosts get to do\" version this section used to describe - it shipped bleaker, and on\r\npurpose (corrected 2026-08-22, prose wins on facts): \"Yes,\" and then no line to draw one with -\r\n\"No original. No root. Just the ghosts, all the way down.\" **There is no discrete self left to\r\npoint to. The composite goes all the way through.** This is a harder answer than empowering\r\nself-authorship, and it is more consonant with the book\u0027s own grief-not-triumph spine (§13h)\r\nthan the version this section previously described.\r\n\r\n### 13c. The \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eStreet Samurai\u003c/entity\u003e distinction {#SS-BCODA-13c}\r\n\r\nThis is the title\u0027s meaning. Not a warrior in a city. A person who has taken what is real from\r\nthe code and stripped the religion away from it.\r\n\r\n**Samurai (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s version):** Honor as constraint. Rules as identity. The code as the man.\r\n\r\n**\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eStreet Samurai\u003c/entity\u003e (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s version, earned late):** Competence as constant. Rules as tools. The\r\ncode in service of survival. Calling \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e because she is better at three things he needs and\r\nthe code\u0027s objection is not load-bearing anymore.\r\n\r\n**But do not write this as a triumph.** \"\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eStreet Samurai\u003c/entity\u003e\" is what\u0027s left after the amputations,\r\nnot a promotion. He is more effective and less whole. The mood is grief (§13h).\r\n\r\n### 13d. The arc\u0027s progression through the book {#SS-BCODA-13d}\r\n\r\n| Phase | Chapters | Virtue falling | What it costs \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **Intact** | Ch1-3 | none | The baseline. He bows, fights clean, tells the truth. |\r\n| **First stains** | Ch5-11 | Courtesy (Ch5), Mercy (Ch11) | He stops giving the enemy the ceremony; steps to survive a killing shot, and it finds a stranger instead. |\r\n| **The private lie** | Ch14 | Honesty | He hides his dying from \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e and sustains it. |\r\n| **The dirty work** | Ch16-18 | Rectitude, Loyalty (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e revealed fabricated — masterless) | Identity crisis. |\r\n| **Choosing to live** | The Floor Is Hard | Courage-to-die | He surrenders the readiness to die clean and chooses to keep existing - for her. |\r\n| **The last stain** | 35th \u0026 Halsted | Honor | He wins the way the code forbids - the feigned surrender, then the blind hand-kill (the single dishonor beat as shipped; amended 2026-07-18, see §13g row 7). |\r\n| **The coda** | One Knock | - | Nothing left to spend. The dirtied man, alive, goes to dinner. |\r\n\r\n### 13e. Implementation rules for combat beats {#SS-BCODA-13e}\r\n\r\n1. **Mark the code-cost moments.** Every time \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e takes damage he didn\u0027t have to take, the\r\n   reader should be able to identify the code-decision that produced it. Not announced - felt.\r\n2. **Do not rehabilitate the code.** The code is not wrong because it is bad. It is wrong because\r\n   it is not \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s.\r\n3. **The code runs harder under pressure.** Before Ch18, when \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e is most stressed, he becomes\r\n   most code-rigid.\r\n4. **Late-book \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e fights different.** The discipline is still there - it was always his. But\r\n   the framing changes. He stops asking \"what does the code require\" and starts asking \"what does\r\n   the situation need.\"\r\n5. **The beacon scene is the proof.** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e goes off-grid to protect \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e \"by the code.\" \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\r\n   arrives anyway. The code prescribed the wrong answer.\r\n\r\n### 13g. The seven touchstones (AUTHORITATIVE — author decision, 2026-07-13; row 7 amended 2026-07-18) {#SS-BCODA-13g}\r\n\r\nSeven resonant moments, one per virtue, in fixed order. **Honor falls last, at 35th \u0026 Halsted\r\n(penultimate chapter); The Floor Is Hard is the hinge.** Each touchstone must satisfy all four tests:\r\n1. **Forced.** \u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"019d6143-a927-73ac-abfa-37c77f9cff8d\"\u003eGLMZ\u003c/entity\u003e leaves no clean option.\r\n2. **For someone.** The stain is paid to keep a specific loved one clean/safe/alive.\r\n3. **A real loss.** Drop to SORROW-grade on the abandonment itself.\r\n4. **Shown, never named.** No \"bushido,\" no \"virtue,\" no lecture.\r\n\r\n| # | Virtue (internal only) | Chapter | The dirtying act | Kept clean |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1 | **Courtesy** - the bow, the announced draw | Ch5 The Carousel | He does not bow, does not announce. The shotgun answers first. | The carousel\u0027s children; bystanders |\r\n| 2 | **Mercy** - the clean kill, the step *around* the civilian line | Ch11 The One Who Doesn\u0027t Stop | He steps clear of a killing shot aimed at him; it carries through and kills a stranger instead. He disarms the man responsible rather than killing him. | an ambulance driver, unchosen; the leader, spared |\r\n| 3 | **Honesty** - sincerity, the truth owed to one\u0027s own | Ch14 One Shoe / Ch15 The Same Secret | He hides his dying from \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e and sustains the omission. | \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e - she doesn\u0027t carry his death |\r\n| 4 | **Rectitude** - justice, \u003centity repo=\"entertainment\" guid=\"019d6513-b76e-734f-9702-c716a9412f2e\"\u003eclean hands\u003c/entity\u003e in the work | Ch16 The Offer — Ch18 Work Order | He leverages a near-innocent (Dae-ho \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f43b9-5ea8-74cd-b722-60e0b4780b9f\"\u003eYim\u003c/entity\u003e) and takes the unjust job. | the crew - the intel keeps them breathing |\r\n| 5 | **Loyalty** - fealty to the master, to \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e | Ch18 Work Order (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"01a02d38-185c-7752-b83e-baa921571078\"\u003eSeito\u003c/entity\u003e revealed fabricated) | The master never existed. He becomes ronin - masterless, by choice. | \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e - protected by his judgment, not the code\u0027s |\r\n| 6 | **Courage-to-die** - the \u003centity repo=\"vocabulary\" guid=\"019d6143-aafb-7b6b-bcbc-b8614f9d228f\"\u003esamurai\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s readiness to die clean | The Floor Is Hard | He surrenders the honorable death and *chooses to keep living* - for her. | \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e - he stays alive to keep standing between her and the city |\r\n| 7 | **Honor** - the last, most iconic | 35th \u0026 Halsted (penultimate) | He wins the way the code forbids: the feigned-surrender hand-kill. Shipped as the single realized violation - the originally-drafted triad (booby-trap + blind kill + ungoverned neuretic sledgehammer) was reduced to this one beat during drafting; the author accepted the leaner climax as complete on its own (BCODA-2, 2026-07-18) and this row records the shipped scope, not the abandoned triad. | everyone - the Schism closes |\r\n\r\n**Continuity of the descent.** After each touchstone the abandoned virtue *stays* abandoned.\r\nPost-Ch5 he no longer bows to what he kills. Post-Ch12 he no longer steps around the line.\r\nThe losses accrue; they do not reset.\r\n\r\n**Do not over-signpost.** At most one touchstone per movement, and never a beat that stops to\r\nunderline it. If a reader on first pass thinks \"ah, a virtue just fell,\" it is too loud.\r\n\r\n### 13h. The last page - what the reader closes the book feeling (author decision, 2026-07-13) {#SS-BCODA-13h}\r\n\r\n**Author\u0027s target:** *\"It\u0027s tearing me apart knowing \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e has to destroy who he is to become\r\nwhat he needs to be. Make sure that\u0027s what resonates on the last page when the reader closes\r\nthe book.\"*\r\n\r\nOne Knock is the coda after the coda. What is left is a man who spent himself down to nothing\r\nto keep the people he loves clean, and the last image must land that cost as **grief, not triumph.**\r\n\r\n**Rules for the closing beat:**\r\n- **No victory posture.** He won; the prose does not celebrate.\r\n- **She does not know the price - and that is the point.** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e comes through the wall with\r\n  the warm soldering iron. She sees the man. She cannot see the ledger of everything he stopped\r\n  being so that she would never have to. His keeping it from her is the last mercy he has left\r\n  to give, and it is the loneliest thing in the book. **This is the resonance** - she asks\r\n  *You eat?* and he says no and they go, and the reader knows what she doesn\u0027t.\r\n- **One flat interior line, colder than the chapter, then white space.** Do not explain the grief.\r\n  Name nothing.\r\n- **Not despair - depletion with one warm point.** \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e is the single thing the dismantling was\r\n  *for*, and she is real, and she is here. The warmth is what makes the grief land (CODA law).\r\n\r\n## 14. Open plant / payoff ledger {#SS-BCODA-14}\r\n\r\n### 14a. Closed plants (payoff written)\r\n\r\n| Plant | Plant location | Payoff | Payoff location | Closed |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Alley figure\u0027s left hand runs 3° colder, unexplained at first (echoes \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s own new diagnosis at SK:2000, a separate thematic parallel) | Ch14 SK:18000 | \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e recognizes the \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019ee6a2-a172-7f5a-9451-03c4c3fe001b\"\u003eContinuity Office\u003c/entity\u003e surveillance asset wore Femi\u0027s stolen biometric signature as a thermal spoofing mask | Ch14 SK:21100 | 2026-07-10 |\r\n| Vulture fledglings throw schism-frequency interference rounds (17-19 Hz) | Ch12 SK:17000 | \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e finds \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"34e17863-d822-4bed-a972-3649099b2444\"\u003ePraxis\u003c/entity\u003e ordnance casings at 35th \u0026 Halsted perimeter - same batch stamp | 35th and Halsted SK:5000 | 2026-07-10 |\r\n\r\n### 14b. Dropped findings\r\n\r\n| Finding | Reason dropped | Date |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Imani registers \"recognition\" at 35th \u0026 Halsted Schism | No causal grounding; line removed per user decision | 2026-07-10 |\r\n| BRING THE SWORD summons card / stolen-sword mystery (Ch30, beats 3195 \u0026 3199) | Logic-sweep 2026-08-01 (m4): \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s sword is confirmed stolen from his locker with a threatening card; by Ch22 he\u0027s using \u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"019ed39c-6321-7c51-9691-f59b441b0bec\"\u003eSilence\u003c/entity\u003e again with zero on-page explanation of recovery or who sent the card. Not a one-clause fix - needs either a resolution beat or an explicit author note. **CLOSED 2026-08-03** - resolution beat spliced on-page: at the Narrows ramen-ya, before the togishi read, the \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019eb6ea-84c8-7ad6-89f8-32630940e563\"\u003eBranch\u003c/entity\u003e Manager returns \u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"019ed39c-6321-7c51-9691-f59b441b0bec\"\u003eSilence\u003c/entity\u003e (\"The borrowing was a question. You answered it by coming.\"). The empty-locker discovery (beat 3195, SortKey 400) and the return (beat 3199, SortKey 800) and all later sword usage now reconcile; the borrower reads as \u003centity repo=\"faction\" guid=\"019d6143-a893-7801-860b-0eda6a216393\"\u003eLotus\u003c/entity\u003e (five-petal card, their venue) without being stated. Citation corrected 2026-08-15: this scene is in **Ch30 \"\u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"019d6143-a948-7b0e-9b15-63f753f313c9\"\u003eThe Narrows\u003c/entity\u003e,\"** not Ch21 - the \"Ch21 SK80000\" label predates the 2026-08-14 reparenting that split Ch21-35 out from under a mislabeled \"Ghost Period\" wrapper. | 2026-08-01 |\r\n\r\n## 15. Brand Environment \u0026 Character Loadout {#SS-BCODA-brands}\r\n\r\nBCODA is complete (V19.docx exported 2026-07-10); this section is canonical for all future\r\nstories featuring \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle Ellen Corbin\u003c/entity\u003e.\r\n\r\n### \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle Ellen Corbin\u003c/entity\u003e - Canonical Loadout\r\n\r\n| Item | Brand / Model | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Motorcycle | **Aries Viper Predator MDK-2** (\u0027Aries\u0027 = the corponation; \u0027Viper\u0027 = the motorcycle line; \u0027Predator\u0027 = \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s model), Matte Black, model year 2215, H-Cell powered (universal power source; hydrogen implied, never confirmed in-universe) - full arc: stolen by a 14-year-old (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e, Ch18 Work Order) and impounded the same night before \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e could ride it home; recovered via \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s 3-month-dormant beacon in the Ch21 Park Job coda after a circuitous impound-to-auction chain, the SAME original bike, not a replacement; destroyed in The Relay Station (Ch34) - the entity drives it autonomously into a recovery truck via \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s ignition handshake, without \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s consent, to save \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e, with 0.4 seconds of margin; mourned at a crew funeral at \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s counter, after which \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e rides the \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"0d831459-182f-4efc-9920-bdf9e032c61d\"\u003ePulse\u003c/entity\u003e to every job for three weeks (\u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"019ed39c-6321-7c51-9691-f59b441b0bec\"\u003eSilence\u003c/entity\u003e sheathed across his back, to the visible horror of Bridgeport grandmothers) while the crew rebuilds it in secret - \u003centity repo=\"person\" guid=\"806cd358-6413-426b-a42d-19726b732c0b\"\u003eVo Dinh\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s shop trues the salvaged frame straight, \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019eb6eb-6eb0-7176-9136-790a0ed124fb\"\u003eGantry\u003c/entity\u003e repaints it (all five crew wet-sanding between coats), \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e rebuilds the ignition handshake and hides a beacon; revealed via a fake-emergency \"unveiling\" (\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-04fb-7227-94d9-6b4d889ce52b\"\u003eBoost\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s operation, staged as an \"ARRIVE ARMED\" page so \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e believes it\u0027s a threat) on the evening of \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s unmarked, unmentioned birthday, and christened \u0027MK. 2\u0027 by \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e himself, in The Acquisition Program (Ch35); gone again by Ch38 (One Knock), cause deliberately unresolved (see SS-BCODA-1c - the entity\u0027s quiet channel on \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e, closing out once the loop resolves). *(Beacon dormancy and rebuild/reveal details corrected 2026-08-15 after Ch21-35 reparenting made this content readable for the first time - the previous \"3-year-dormant\" and \"\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-c1d5-e7f8-a92b-34068c150e4d\"\u003ePixel\u003c/entity\u003e alone rebuilds\"/\"surprise birthday party\" wording did not match the shipped prose.)* | \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019f524d-ec65-703b-871f-45cc8e7aca85\"\u003eAries Performance Vehicles\u003c/entity\u003e (\u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a018a4-086e-73c5-b9ca-65a52a73f25c\"\u003ePilsen\u003c/entity\u003e); eigenlift stabilization - applies to the original only |\r\n| Sword | **\u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"019ed39c-6321-7c51-9691-f59b441b0bec\"\u003eSilence\u003c/entity\u003e** | No brand - just a sword (SS-LAW-10). The absence of branding is the point. |\r\n| Shotgun | **Torii Security Group TSS-3 \u0027\u003centity repo=\"weapon\" guid=\"4ab24f74-61d4-4f45-b326-7c6b98c96279\"\u003eCacophony\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027** | Six-shot revolver shotgun; \u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019d6143-a648-7876-9688-0f6d38d70075\"\u003eKyle\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s personal name (for the sound it makes). |\r\n| \u003centity repo=\"technology\" guid=\"019f0464-2fee-725a-a5e0-00628447b431\"\u003eNeuretics\u003c/entity\u003e | **Atlas NeoCortex** (Sovereign tier, ungoverned) | No governor - is killing him. |\r\n| Apparel | **Gray zone reclaim** - black duster over technical base layer | No archology brand by choice. The absence of visible branding IS the brand signal. |\r\n\r\n### Setting Brand Environment\r\n\r\nBCODA is set primarily in the Loop, Bloom Quarter, and gray zones adjacent to both.\r\n\r\n- **\u003centity repo=\"place\" guid=\"01a01887-b5f4-781c-8d38-122f7e1f38ba\"\u003eThe Loop\u003c/entity\u003e** - \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019f524f-a312-75d5-af6e-7271b67cde43\"\u003eCasque \u0026 Veil\u003c/entity\u003e on every executive; \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019d6143-a7b6-7f75-85fe-75609a103282\"\u003eWaxwing Neuromedia\u003c/entity\u003e ad-impressions; \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019d6143-a7a4-71f6-b46a-94ef8cb2348f\"\u003eArcturus\u003c/entity\u003e kinetic interceptor systems on every rooftop\r\n- **Gray zone** - \u003centity repo=\"corponation\" guid=\"019f524f-d1ca-7ddd-9420-70fdd25ace0f\"\u003eGreymark Unseen\u003c/entity\u003e; CDW weapons; Aries bikes; CramIt bars; street-custom everything else\r\n- **\u003centity repo=\"character\" guid=\"019f441d-3404-79c2-a8f6-2942f504698e\"\u003eMrs. Chen\u003c/entity\u003e\u0027s stall** - unlicensed, unbranded, real food; the one thing in the story that has no commercial origin story\r\n"